XB-Kidux-Name-en: Gmail
XB-Kidux-Description-en: The Gmail website for a Google account, including one managed with Family Link. Requires internet; an adult signs in with the child the first time, and the session stays. Kidux is not connected with Google.
XB-Kidux-Name-es: Gmail
XB-Kidux-Description-es: La web de Gmail para una cuenta de Google, también una supervisada con Family Link. Requiere internet; un adulto inicia sesión con el niño la primera vez, y la sesión se mantiene. Kidux no tiene ninguna relación con Google.
XB-Kidux-Ages: 8-
Description: Kidux learning module: Gmail, a door to Gmail's website
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This learning
 module opens Gmail's website in a window of its own, and no other
 website: a link to anywhere else leads nowhere. Nothing of Gmail is in
 this package; the site, the mail and the account are Google's.
 .
 It needs the internet and a Google account. It is the module for a child
 whose Google account is managed with Family Link, which Google does not
 let sign in to a mail program; an adult signs in with the child the first
 time, and the session stays.
 .
 Kidux and its author have no connection with Google.
 .
 Once it is installed, an adult switches it on for each child on the
 Modules page of the adult panel.
